<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ may exempt over 60s from super at first - Peters.</title>
<headline>NZ may exempt over 60s from super at first - Peters.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Treasurer Winston Peters said on Friday that if New Zealand goes ahead with its proposed compulsory superannuation scheme people aged 60 and over on the start-up date might be exempted from contributing to the scheme.</p>
</text>
